C("DLS26 supports 15 languages (App Store/Press): English, Arabic, Dutch, French, German, Indonesian, Italian, Japanese, Korean, Portuguese, Russian, Simplified Chinese, Spanish, Traditional Chinese, Turkish. Commentary languages confirmed: English (original), Spanish (added DLS24), Portuguese (added DLS25), Turkish + Arabic (added Summer Spotlight 13.410, July 2026) = 5 commentary tracks.",'High Confidence',[e288,'EV-280'])
C("Age rating: 13+ (Apple). Contains frequent contests + loot boxes + advertising. Free-to-play with IAP.",'High Confidence',[e288])
C("Custom kit/logo import technical specs: 512×512 pixels exactly, PNG preferred (JPG/WebP accepted), transparent background recommended, file size under 1MB, served from a direct hotlink-enabled URL ending in .png/.jpg/.webp (Google Drive/Dropbox links fail — game fetches them as webpages). Kit slots: Home/Away/Third/GK. Logo same spec. Kit must conform to official UV-mapped template layout (front/back/sleeves/shorts zones) or decals mis-map (e.g. sponsor on sleeve/back instead of chest).",'High Confidence',[e289])
C("Custom kit/logo import is a feature that must be UNLOCKED with a 150-gem one-time purchase before paste-URL entry works.",'High Confidence',[e289])
C("DLS26 gameplay tuning evolution (post-launch, community timeline): Launch Dec 2025 — slower pace, momentum/inertia-based passing (more realistic), C-button (loft pass/cross) nerfed, control/passing/tackling stats elevated in value vs raw speed (reduced fitness-coach meta), improved tiki-taka buildup/dribbling, reduced scripting but worse player switching, GKs unpredictable, 'stats feel placebo' complaints; Within ~2 weeks post-launch a patch REVERTED passing toward DLS25 physics (easier/assisted) because users complained passes were too hard; AI was then perceived as too easy ('useless') with long shots less effective than DLS25; Legendary Division remains significantly harder than lower divisions throughout.",'Community Consensus',[e290],['Subjective community reports across multiple Reddit threads; no official patch notes for tuning changes.'],vol='High')
C("AI difficulty / 'handicap' community perception (DLS26 hard/Legendary): (a) AI wins 50/50s and tackles 'artificially' (high-CON players dispossessed by low-TAC AI; 189cm/80+STR CBs lose aerial duels to shorter/lower-rated forwards); (b) user's players 'miss simple short passes' and inputs produce unnatural power; (c) AI presses aggressively and receiving players freeze/run away from the ball causing interceptions; (d) GKs inconsistent (Donnarumma-tier can't stop tame shots, sometimes don't react); (e) AI can play ultra-deep block (8 men behind ball in 4-2-3-1 high-press, Legendary) that forces skill-move abuse; (f) AI 'reads inputs' / reacts before user animation completes (perennial complaint). These are widely-reported subjective perceptions — not independently confirmed as intentional scripting/handicap code.",'Community Consensus',[e290],['Subjective reports; difficult to distinguish from AI sliders, latency, physics bugs, or confirmation bias.'],vol='High')
C("DLS26 launch positives cited by community: less opponent 'lag', improved tiki-taka build-up AI, improved dribbling, reduced (not eliminated) match scripting, slower pace rewarding control/passing/tackling over pace spam.",'Community Consensus',[e290],vol='Medium')
C("Ads reward ~30-40 coins per video ad view (DLS26); no confirmed daily cap on ad views.",'Community Consensus',[e288],['Ad reward magnitude and availability may vary by region/update.'],vol='Medium')
